00:48:23,225 --> 00:48:29,225
Batman & Robin is a 1997 American superhero film based on the DC Comics
characters Batman and Robin by Bill Finger and Bob Kane.

13
00:52:25,161 --> 00:52:31,161
It is the fourth and final installment of Warner Bros.' initial Batman film
series (1989–1997) and a sequel to Batman Forever (1995).

14
00:56:27,096 --> 00:56:33,096
Directed by Joel Schumacher and written by Akiva Goldsman, it stars George Clooney as Bruce Wayne / Batman and Chris
O'Donnell as Dick Grayson / Robin, alongside Arnold Schwarzenegger, Uma Thurman, and Alicia Silverstone.

15
01:00:29,032 --> 01:00:35,032
The film follows the titular characters as they oppose Mr.

16
01:04:30,967 --> 01:04:36,967
Freeze and Poison Ivy, while struggling to keep their partnership together.

17
01:08:32,903 --> 01:08:38,903
Warner Bros.

18
01:12:34,838 --> 01:12:40,838
fast-tracked development for Batman & Robin following the box office success of Batman Forever;
Schumacher was given a mandate to make the film more toyetic than its predecessor.

19
01:16:36,774 --> 01:16:42,774
Schumacher and Goldsman conceived the storyline
during pre-production on A Time to Kill.

20
01:20:38,709 --> 01:20:44,709
After Val Kilmer decided not to reprise the role of Batman, Schumacher was
interested in casting William Baldwin before Clooney won the role.

21
01:24:40,645 --> 01:24:46,645
Principal photography began in September 1996 and wrapped in
January 1997, two weeks ahead of the shooting schedule.

22
01:28:42,580 --> 01:28:48,580
Batman & Robin is the only film in the initial Batman film series made
without the involvement of Tim Burton in any capacity.

23
01:32:44,516 --> 01:32:50,516
Batman & Robin premiered in Los Angeles on June 12, 1997,
and went into general release on June 20.

24
01:36:46,451 --> 01:36:52,451
It grossed $238 million worldwide against a production budget of $125–160
million, and was considered a box office disappointment at the time.

25
